#: ../../../subprocess.rst:267
msgid "What all this means:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:269
msgid ""
"**Blocking** -- whether xonsh waits for the process to finish before "
"continuing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:271
msgid ""
"**Capture stdout** -- whether stdout is captured into a ``CommandPipeline`` "
"object instead of being streamed to the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:273
msgid ""
"**Capture stderr** -- whether stderr is captured into a ``CommandPipeline`` "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:274
msgid ""
"**TTY input** -- whether the process receives terminal input (stdin). "
"Without it, interactive tools (e.g. ``fzf``, ``vim``) will be suspended by "
"the OS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:277
msgid ""
"**TTY output** -- whether stdout is connected directly to the terminal. \"no "
"(threadable)\" means the stream is redirected for threadable processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:280
msgid ""
"**Raise** -- whether a non-zero return code raises ``CalledProcessError`` "
"(when ``$RAISE_SUBPROC_ERROR`` is ``True``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:282
msgid "**Returns** -- the Python type of the value returned by the operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../subprocess.rst:284
msgid ""
"A **thread** (threadable, capturable) process is one that does not interact "
"with the user. If an unthreadable process runs with a detached terminal it "
"will be suspended by the OS automatically."
msgstr ""

